@startuml

title The lifecycle of one party fixing

hide empty description

state "Required" as required
state "Dormant" as dormant
state "Unofficial" as unofficial
state "Official" as official

[*] --> required : a trade of the party subscribes\nto the source for this date

required --> dormant : the party keys a value\nin advance of the fixing date
dormant --> unofficial : every earlier fixing of the source\nis official for the party

required --> unofficial : the source's observation arrives,\nor the party keys a value

unofficial --> unofficial : overkeyed by the party\n(the observation is kept)

unofficial --> official : authorised by the party's operations\n(raises a fix event)
official --> unofficial : unauthorised or undone\n(raises an undo event)

official --> [*] : no live trade of the party\nrequires it any more

note right of unofficial
    front office may key or overkey;
    only the party's operations may authorise,
    and only after the publication time
end note

note right of official
    the observation itself has no status:
    another party may hold it as unofficial
end note

@enduml
